# Streaming minibatches

Chunk streams follow the stored grid. DataLoader batches follow the first axis and can cross chunk boundaries.

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:ex_zarr, "~> 1.3"},
  # {:ex_zarr, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "../../..")},
  {:nx, "~> 0.7"}
])
```

## Data

```elixir
alias ExZarr.Array

{:ok, features} =
  Array.create(shape: {10, 4}, chunks: {4, 4}, dtype: :float32, storage: :memory)

{:ok, labels} =
  Array.create(shape: {10}, chunks: {4}, dtype: :float32, storage: :memory)

x = for i <- 0..39, into: <<>>, do: <<i * 1.0::float-little-32>>
y = for i <- 0..9, into: <<>>, do: <<i * 1.0::float-little-32>>
:ok = Array.set_slice(features, x, start: {0, 0}, stop: {10, 4})
:ok = Array.set_slice(labels, y, start: {0}, stop: {10})

:ok
```

## One tensor per stored chunk

The last chunk is shorter than `{4, 4}`. `stream_chunk_tensors/2` crops it.

```elixir
features
|> ExZarr.Nx.stream_chunk_tensors(concurrency: 2, ordered: true)
|> Enum.map(fn {:ok, tensor} -> Nx.shape(tensor) end)
```

## Fixed-size batches

```elixir
features
|> ExZarr.Nx.DataLoader.batch_stream(3, drop_remainder: true)
|> Enum.map(fn {:ok, batch} -> Nx.shape(batch) end)
```

## Paired and shuffled batches

Shuffling uses the full sample index. `:shuffle_buffer_size` is ignored. `:seed` makes the order repeatable.

```elixir
ExZarr.Nx.DataLoader.paired_shuffled_batch_stream(features, labels, 4, seed: 1)
|> Enum.map(fn {:ok, {xb, yb}} -> {Nx.shape(xb), Nx.shape(yb)} end)
```
